 "_notes": {
  "method": [
   "python3 scripts/analyze_tree.py            -> writes data/params/tree.json (numpy/scipy only, world metres)",
   "",
   "Method",
   "- Bark splats: opacity > 100, not green-dominant, low saturation (grey-brown), inside a box around the trunk that",
   "  was located by back-projecting the hero-frame trunk pixels (u 480-590, v 20-200) to their depth cluster",
   "  (4.0-4.8 m): the cluster sits at world (0.05, -2.6), i.e. -Y of the table, behind it in the hero view.",
   "- Each stem is traced upward in 0.1 m slices: an algebraic (Kasa) circle fit on the slice's XY gives the centre",
   "  (the scan covers ~200-300 deg of the circumference, so the centre is constrained); the radius is the half",
   "  5-95 % X extent, which is what the hero silhouette shows (the hero camera looks almost along -Y).",
   "- Control points are a least-squares quadratic (x, y in z) and linear radius through the slice fits, sampled at a",
   "  few heights; above the scan ceiling (~2.4 m: the capture never saw higher) the stems are extrapolated and",
   "  marked as unseen.",
   "- Ground at the base: low percentile of splat z in rings around the trunk.",
   "- Crown: foliage splats above 1.9 m within 1.6 m of the trunk axis; the scan stops at 2.7 m, so the crown height",
   "  and top are an assumption (marked) and only its lower envelope is measured."
  ],
  "trunk": "slice fits z 0.2-0.9 (rms centre residual 0.012 m); radius = median circle-fit radius of 0.3-0.85 m slices (checked against the hero silhouette half-width 0.19-0.21 m; axis shifted +0.033 m X to match the hero edges) (0.184 m), +35 % flare to the ground. Uncertainty ~+-0.02 m.",
  "stems": "main/left/right stems traced in 0.1 m slices to the scan ceiling (~2.3 m); rms residuals 0.007/0.016/0.016 m. Points above 2.35 m are extrapolated (unseen: no splats above 2.7 m anywhere in the scan).",
